B.I6=new A.id("Why are you interested in this role at Acme Labs?","Acme's mobile + web cross-platform brief is exactly the surface I've been shipping for the last five years \u2014 Flutter on iOS, Android, and Web from a single repo. Your design-system rewrite caught my eye because it maps onto a Material 2 \u2192 Material 3 collapse I led in 2024 (eight legacy surfaces into one token-driven system, ~40% faster screen builds). I'd want to bring that pattern to Acme.")
B.Ic=new A.id(u._,"At Bytewave I led the migration of a fintech app with 80k+ DAU from native Android + iOS into a single Flutter codebase. Beyond the rewrite I introduced a CI/CD pipeline on GitHub Actions + Firebase App Distribution that cut release cycle time from 2 weeks to 2 days, and built native platform channels for biometric auth and camera-stream OCR where Flutter plugins weren't enough. Cross-platform parity, native fallbacks, and a release cadence the business could plan around \u2014 that was the brief and it landed.")
B.I5=new A.id(u.a,"Flutter + Dart is my primary stack since 2021. Riverpod and BLoC for state, GoRouter for routing, Firebase + Supabase as backends across recent projects. Native channels in Swift and Kotlin where I've needed to reach BLE, camera, or biometrics. CI: GitHub Actions, Firebase App Distribution, golden-image visual regression. Where I'm thinner is Flutter desktop \u2014 I've prototyped but not shipped to production.")
B.Ia=new A.id("How do you approach leading a design-system rewrite?","Start by inventorying the existing surfaces and counting the actual variants in use \u2014 almost always smaller than the design team thinks. Land tokens (color, type, spacing, radius) before components, so the visual layer is already aligned when components ship. Migrate one product surface end-to-end as a reference, then peel the rest in PRs the team can review independently. I keep a 'co-existence' phase where old and new can sit side by side; ripping the bandaid all at once is what kills these efforts.")
B.I4=new A.id(u.Z,"Available with 2\u20134 weeks notice from current role; flexible on start date and happy to overlap during a handover.")
B.I9=new A.id(u.i,"Berlin works well for me \u2014 I'm in a +1/-1 hour timezone today and would relocate or split-time happily. Hybrid or fully on-site both fine.")
B.UF=s([B.I6,B.Ic,B.I5,B.Ia,B.I4,B.I9],t.gx)
B.UJ=s([0,0.85,1],t.n)
B.a19=new A.af("Overview","This policy explains what data JobPilot collects, why, and your choices. We aim to collect only what the service needs to work.")
B.a1i=new A.af("What we collect","Account data: your email address and password (passwords are handled by our authentication provider and never stored by us in plain text).\n\nProfile data you provide: your name, phone, location, links, search profiles, and any CV files you upload.\n\nGenerated data: job matches and AI-drafted application materials tied to your account.\n\nUsage analytics: anonymous, aggregated product-usage events (for example, \u201ca draft was generated\u201d) so we can understand and improve the product.")
B.a0Y=new A.af("How we use it","We use your data to operate the service: to scrape and match jobs against your profiles, to generate tailored drafts, and to show you your history. We use aggregated analytics to improve features and fix problems. We do not sell your personal data.")
B.a1b=new A.af("Third-party processors","To run the service we rely on: Supabase (database, authentication, and file storage); AI providers (such as OpenRouter, Google Gemini, and Groq) which process the text needed to generate your drafts; job-board and enrichment APIs (such as Adzuna, Jooble, RemoteOK, and Brandfetch) to source listings; and PostHog for product analytics. These providers process data on our behalf under their own security and privacy terms.")
B.a1j=new A.af("Data retention and deletion","We keep your data while your account is active. You can permanently delete your account and its data at any time from Settings \u2192 Danger zone; deletion cascades through your profile, search profiles, CVs, and drafts. Some anonymised, aggregated analytics that cannot identify you may be retained.")
B.a0K=new A.af("Your choices","You can view and edit your profile and applicant details in Settings, remove uploaded CVs, pause all automation, and delete your account. For any data request, contact support@jobpilot.example.")
B.a0F=new A.af("Security","Access to your data is restricted by row-level security so each account can only reach its own records. No system is perfectly secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security, but we take reasonable measures to protect your information.")
B.a1d=new A.af("Changes to this policy","We may update this policy as the product evolves. Material changes will be reflected in the \u201clast updated\u201d date above.")
B.UK=s([B.a19,B.a1i,B.a0Y,B.a1b,B.a1j,B.a0K,B.a0F,B.a1d],t.Wy)
