B.I1=new A.id("Why are you interested in this role at Bloomwire?","Small-team B2C Flutter on Firebase is the most leverage-per-engineer setup I know \u2014 short feedback loops, real product impact, and the right stack for fast iteration. I've shipped four production Flutter apps including one on a similar Firebase backend, and the 'help us ship' framing in the JD reads like the kind of hands-on role I do my best work in.")
B.I3=new A.id(u._,"Last year I led the Material 2 \u2192 Material 3 design-system rewrite at Plurality: collapsed eight legacy surfaces into a token-driven system, cut new-screen build time by ~40%, and onboarded two junior engineers into shared ownership of the system. The win wasn't the visual refresh \u2014 it was that the next quarter's feature work landed twice as fast because the team stopped re-deciding spacing and color every PR.")
B.I2=new A.id(u.a,"Flutter + Firebase since 2022 \u2014 Auth, Firestore, Functions, App Distribution, Crashlytics. Riverpod for state, GoRouter for routing. I've also wired native channels in Swift and Kotlin when Flutter plugins were thin. Where the JD touches REST + GraphQL, I've consumed both from Flutter clients with codegen pipelines.")
B.I7=new A.id("How do you approach early-stage product velocity?","Pick the boring stack on day one \u2014 Flutter, Firebase, GitHub Actions \u2014 so you spend zero brain budget on infra. Ship behind feature flags; the only thing slower than a half-built feature is a half-rolled-back one. Keep one engineer-day a week for paying down the tech debt the velocity creates, otherwise month three becomes a swamp.")
B.I8=new A.id(u.Z,"Available with 2 weeks notice; can start sooner for the right team.")
B.Ib=new A.id(u.i,"Fully remote works well \u2014 I keep CET hours by default and overlap 4\u20136 hours daily with US-East teams when needed.")
B.Wq=s([B.I1,B.I3,B.I2,B.I7,B.I8,B.Ib],t.gx)
