s($,"bGM","bkN",()=>{var q="Flutter Developer",p="Senior Flutter Developer",o=null,n="Python Backend Engineer",m="Remote",l="DevOps Engineer",k="Data Engineer"
return A.b([A.zk(B.UF,"acmelabs.example","c-acme","https://logo.clearbit.com/acmelabs.com","Hi Acme Labs hiring team,\n\nI'm writing about the Senior Flutter Developer role on your mobile + web initiative. Over the last five years I've shipped four production Flutter apps \u2014 including a fintech client used by 80k+ daily users \u2014 and I've owned the cross-platform architecture in three of them, which is exactly what your role calls for.\n\nThe design-system rewrite jumped out at me. At my last role I led a similar effort, collapsing eight legacy Material 2 surfaces into a token-driven Material 3 system; we cut new-screen build time by ~40% and onboarded two junior devs into shared ownership of the system. I'd be happy to talk about how that went, especially the pieces that didn't.\n\nBerlin works well for me \u2014 I'm in a +1 / -1 hour timezone today and would relocate or split-time happily.\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you,\nSaad\n",A.Ta(1),o,o,"Strong Flutter background with cross-platform architecture experience and prior design-system leadership \u2014 directly matches the role.",88,"a1","Acme Labs","Acme Labs is looking for a senior Flutter engineer to lead our mobile + web apps.","j1","Berlin, DE",p,u.M,"m1","p1",q,p,o,o,o,B.dR,"SAAD AWAN \u2014 Senior Flutter Engineer\nisaadawan1122@gmail.com  \xb7  GitHub /saadkhanawan  \xb7  Karachi \u2192 relocating EU\n\nEXPERIENCE\nLead Mobile Engineer \xb7 Plurality (remote, 2024\u2013present)\n- Owned cross-platform Flutter codebase shipping to iOS + Android + Web from one repo.\n- Drove a Material 2 \u2192 Material 3 design-system rewrite; new-screen build time -40%.\n- Mentored two junior engineers; introduced golden-image visual regression testing.\n\nSenior Mobile Engineer \xb7 Bytewave (Karachi, 2021\u20132024)\n- Shipped a fintech app with 80k+ DAU; led the migration from native Android + iOS to a single Flutter codebase.\n- Introduced a CI/CD pipeline (GitHub Actions + Firebase App Distribution) cutting release cycle time from 2w \u2192 2d.\n- Built native platform channels for biometric auth + camera-stream OCR.\n\nSKILLS\nFlutter / Dart, Riverpod, BLoC, GoRouter, native iOS (Swift) + Android (Kotlin) channels, GitHub Actions, Firebase, Supabase, REST + GraphQL, BLE.\n"),A.zk(o,"northwind.example",o,"https://logo.clearbit.com/northwind.com","Hi Northwind team,\n\nThe ingestion layer rewrite at Northwind Systems is the kind of problem I look for. I've spent the last three years on data-pipeline platforms \u2014 most recently shipping a Kafka-driven ingestion layer at Bytewave that handled 14k events/sec at p99 \u2014 and the FastAPI + Postgres + event-driven brief in your posting maps neatly onto that work.\n\nA few things I'd want to dig into: how do you handle schema drift between producers and consumers, and what's your current observability story on backpressure? Happy to share my notes from our previous schema-registry rollout if useful.\n\nFully remote and CET-adjacent works for me.\n\nBest,\nSaad\n",A.Ta(3),o,o,"Solid backend Python + Kafka exposure; gap on dedicated FastAPI shop experience but transferable.",71,"a2","Northwind Systems","Build the ingestion layer of our data-pipeline platform. Python 3.12, FastAPI, Postgres, Kafka.","j2",m,n,u.k,"m2","p2","Senior Python Engineer",n,o,o,o,B.dR,"SAAD AWAN \u2014 Backend / Data Engineer\nisaadawan1122@gmail.com  \xb7  GitHub /saadkhanawan\n\nEXPERIENCE\nBackend Engineer \xb7 Bytewave (Karachi, 2022\u2013present)\n- Built ingestion pipeline on FastAPI + Kafka + Postgres handling 14k events/sec at p99.\n- Owned schema-registry rollout across 12 producer services; cut bad-message rate by 78%.\n- Wrote pgbouncer-aware migration tooling so DDL doesn't block oncall.\n\nSKILLS\nPython 3.12, FastAPI, asyncio, SQLAlchemy, Postgres, Kafka, Redis, Docker, observability (OpenTelemetry, Grafana, Loki).\n"),A.zk(o,"cloudforge.example",o,"https://logo.clearbit.com/cloudforge.com","Hi CloudForge team,\n\nThe \"EKS hardening + Terraform Cloud \u2192 Atlantis\" arc you describe is the exact migration I led at my last job, so I'm writing fast. We moved 60+ services off Terraform Cloud onto self-hosted Atlantis with GitHub-app PR reviews; the cost saving paid for the platform team's salaries and the rollback story got a lot calmer.\n\nStrong AWS, Kubernetes, and incident response are all in the toolbox. EU-remote works well \u2014 I keep CET hours by default.\n\nCheers,\nSaad\n",A.Ta(6),o,o,"EKS + Terraform exposure aligns; less recent hands-on with Atlantis specifically.",46,"a3","CloudForge","Harden EKS footprint and lead the move from Terraform Cloud to self-managed Atlantis.","j5",m,l,"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/cloudforge-devops","m3","p4",l,l,o,o,o,B.dR,"SAAD AWAN \u2014 Platform / DevOps Engineer\nisaadawan1122@gmail.com\n\nEXPERIENCE\nPlatform Engineer \xb7 Plurality (remote, 2024\u2013present)\n- Migrated 60+ services from Terraform Cloud \u2192 self-hosted Atlantis on EKS.\n- Authored EKS hardening playbook (PSP\u2192PSA, IRSA-only, Karpenter rightsizing).\n- Reduced p95 deploy time from 11m \u2192 3m.\n\nSKILLS\nAWS, EKS, Terraform, Atlantis, Karpenter, Helm, ArgoCD, GitHub Actions, incident response (Pagerduty + post-mortems).\n"),A.zk(B.Wq,"bloomwire.example",o,"https://logo.clearbit.com/bloomwire.com","Hi Bloomwire team,\n\nSmall startup + Flutter + Firebase + remote-first is my exact happy path right now. I've shipped two B2C Flutter-on-Firebase apps end-to-end \u2014 auth, storage, cloud functions, release management \u2014 and I'm comfortable wearing every hat your job description lists.\n\nWhat I'd want to understand early: what's the current crash-free rate on iOS, what's blocking you from raising it, and how aggressive is the equity vs. cash split? Happy to discuss in a 30-minute call if useful.\n\nThanks,\nSaad\n",A.Ta(8),o,o,"Strong Flutter + Firebase fit; remote-first culture aligns with candidate preferences.",81,"a4","Bloomwire","Small startup, big ambitions \u2014 help us ship a B2C Flutter app on top of Firebase.","j11",m,"Flutter + Firebase Developer","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/bloomwire-flutter","m4","p1",q,p,o,o,o,B.dR,"SAAD AWAN \u2014 Flutter + Firebase Engineer\nisaadawan1122@gmail.com  \xb7  Karachi (remote-friendly)\n\nEXPERIENCE\nLead Mobile Engineer \xb7 Plurality (remote, 2024\u2013present)\n- Solo-built a Flutter+Firebase B2C app from scratch; 12k MAU and 99.6% crash-free sessions.\n- Owned the Cloud Functions backend + scheduled jobs + storage rules.\n\nSKILLS\nFlutter / Dart, Firebase Auth/Firestore/Functions/Storage, Crashlytics, GitHub Actions, Supabase, App Store + Play Console release management.\n"),A.zk(o,"quantix.example",o,"https://logo.clearbit.com/quantix.com","Hi Quantix team,\n\nReal-time analytics on Snowflake + dbt + Airflow is what I do every day. I'd love to talk about your pipeline freshness SLAs in particular \u2014 at my last role I shifted us from a \"best-effort hourly\" model to a freshness contract per dataset, which surprisingly cut more on-call pages than any infra change we made that year.\n\nHybrid in Shoreditch is fine; I'd be in 3 days a week.\n\nBest,\nSaad\n",A.Ta(28),o,o,"Direct Snowflake + dbt + Airflow alignment.",84,"a5","Quantix","Build and maintain real-time analytics platform: Snowflake, dbt, Airflow.","j7","London, UK",k,"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/quantix-data","m5","p6",k,k,o,A.Ta(20),"manual",B.d6,"SAAD AWAN \u2014 Data Engineer\nisaadawan1122@gmail.com  \xb7  London (relocating)\n\nEXPERIENCE\nData Engineer \xb7 Plurality (remote, 2024\u2013present)\n- Owned Snowflake + dbt + Airflow stack across 200+ models.\n- Defined per-dataset freshness SLAs; reduced data-incident pages by 41%.\n\nSKILLS\nSnowflake, dbt, Airflow, Python, SQL, Looker, dbt-tests, Great Expectations, AWS.\n")],t.bH)})
